# The till moves to its own subdomain; plutus.huggett.dscloud.me becomes the landing page.
#
# Matt, 2026-08-25: *"Can you make the plutus.huggett.dscloud.me default page the new landing page"*
# and *"New till subdomain please."*
#
# ⚠⚠ APPLY IN TWO STEPS, NOT ONE. Step 1 adds the till's new home while the old one keeps working,
# so there is never a moment with no till. Only once both tills are re-enrolled and trading on the
# new host does step 2 hand the bare host over to the landing page. The full sequence, with the
# re-enrolment and the verification, is in `Build/till-subdomain-cutover.md`.
#
# ⚠ DNS needs nothing: the Synology DDNS wildcard already resolves any depth
# (`till.plutus.huggett.dscloud.me` → 94.6.166.54, verified 2026-08-25). Caddy will get its own
# certificate on first request.
#
# ⚠ Never touch the ETRIE blocks in this file, and re-run the ETRIE health curl after every reload.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 1 — ADD THIS. Nothing else changes; the till now answers on BOTH hosts.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
till.plutus.huggett.dscloud.me {
	encode zstd gzip

	handle /api/* {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5100
	}

	handle {
		root * /srv/apps/PLUTUS/web/current
		try_files {path} /index.html
		file_server
	}

	log {
		output file /var/log/caddy/plutus-till-access.log
		format console
	}
}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 2 — REPLACE the existing `plutus.huggett.dscloud.me { … }` block with this.
#
# ⚠ Only after both tills are trading on till.plutus…, because this is the moment the old URL
#   stops being a till.
# ⚠⚠ `/api/*` STAYS, AND IT IS LOAD-BEARING FOR TWO SEPARATE REASONS. The landing page calls
#   `/api/v1/signup`, `/signup/dpa` and `/signup/dpa/accept` — but far more importantly, **every
#   MAUI till on the estate talks to `/api/*` on THIS bare host** (`TillConnection.DefaultServerUrl`).
#   Removing this proxy on the reasoning that "a marketing page does not need an API" would take the
#   entire native till estate offline, and nothing on this page would look wrong.
# ⚠ The landing dist ships a TOMBSTONE `/sw.js` that unregisters the till's old service worker. It
#   must be served as a real file — which `try_files` does, because the file exists. Do not "tidy"
#   it away: without it the old worker survives, since the SPA fallback would answer 200 with HTML
#   for a missing /sw.js and the browser would keep the worker it already has.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
plutus.huggett.dscloud.me {
	encode zstd gzip

	handle /api/* {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5100
	}

	handle {
		root * /srv/apps/PLUTUS/landing/current
		try_files {path} /index.html
		file_server
	}

	log {
		output file /var/log/caddy/plutus-access.log
		format console
	}
}
